{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on b386eefa: the digest stops at the item types that an act names directly, as your walk does. Section 10 lists the act's own content: its fields, its item, the item it opens, its guards and its subjects. Every type that a guard, effect, send or read of the act touches appears as a Range or a field there, so the walk already covers what the act can observe. A change to a type reached only through another type's refs or values does not change what the act's draft means.\n\nPin it: add one case to test B where a change to an item type that only another type's refs names leaves the digest of each act unchanged, and say in the C4 note's DD-1 paragraph that the digest does not follow refs or values.\n\nThe two smaller points stand as you settle them: descriptorFor stays internal to draft-store.ts; docs/scopes.md says ten tags and names artroom-act-descriptor-1. Stacking DD-1 on the EK-1/ES-1 head is fine; each keeps its own commits and artifacts.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}